From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/PlatformBootManagerLib: No UEFI Shell option
 without the Shell

The boot manager registers the UEFI Shell from the firmware volume at
every boot. BdsGetFvFileDevicePath () finds no volume with the file in a
build without the Shell (SHELL_TYPE NONE), so nothing is registered, but
the option that an earlier firmware with the Shell made stays in
BootOrder and in the boot menu, and only fails when chosen.

Register the Shell when a volume has it, as before; otherwise delete the
options that start its file, as for iPXE and CSMWrap when they are
turned off (PlatformRemoveFvBootOption ()). Nothing changes with the
Shell in the volume.
---
 .../PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c       | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index 3d77b5e8f60..525025906e2 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -766,9 +766,15 @@ PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole (
   }
 
   //
-  // Register UEFI Shell
+  // Register the UEFI Shell if the firmware volume has it; a build without
+  // it (SHELL_TYPE NONE) deletes the option that an older one made, which
+  // would only fail.
   //
-  PlatformRegisterFvBootOption (&gUefiShellFileGuid, L"UEFI Shell", LOAD_OPTION_ACTIVE);
+  if (BdsGetFvFileDevicePath (&gUefiShellFileGuid) != NULL) {
+    PlatformRegisterFvBootOption (&gUefiShellFileGuid, L"UEFI Shell", LOAD_OPTION_ACTIVE);
+  } else {
+    PlatformRemoveFvBootOption (&gUefiShellFileGuid);
+  }
 
